{"title":"Ironvale Plant Hire","sub":"An online rental platform: scale it up or shut it down?","type":"Growth strategy","industry":"Equipment rental","geo":"Australia","diff":3,"fmt":"Candidate-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"Channel economics · cannibalisation · break-even vs market size","prompt":"Ironvale rents construction equipment to builders from 12 depots around Brisbane. A year ago it launched an online booking platform with delivery to site, aimed at small builders. Online orders are growing, but the platform loses money. The board must decide whether to invest more or close it. The CEO asks for your view.","clarify":[{"q":"Order economics?","a":"The average online rental is $380 with a 55% contribution margin before delivery. Delivery and collection cost $95 an order, free to the customer."},{"q":"Marketing?","a":"About $60 to win a new online customer, who then places about 4 orders a year."},{"q":"Platform costs?","a":"$1.2M a year for the platform, support and marketing team."},{"q":"Who orders online?","a":"About 30% of online orders come from builders who used to walk into a depot."},{"q":"Market?","a":"About 9,000 small builders in the delivery area, each renting about 6 times a year."},{"q":"Current volume?","a":"About 4,000 online orders a year, from roughly 1,000 online customers."}],"structure":{"root":"Should Ironvale scale or close the online platform?","branches":[{"head":"Profit per online order","items":["Margin","Delivery","Marketing"]},{"head":"Cannibalisation","items":["Orders that would have come to a depot anyway"]},{"head":"Break-even","items":["Orders needed vs the market"]},{"head":"Levers","items":["Delivery fee","Fixed cost"]}]},"hypothesis":"Free delivery takes a big bite out of each order, and some online orders are depot customers switching, which adds nothing. The break-even could be out of reach unless delivery is charged.","questions":[{"q":"What does a new online order earn, and how many orders would break even?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Contribution: 55% × $380 = $209. Less delivery $95 and marketing $60 ÷ 4 orders = $15: <b>$99 per order</b>.</p> <p>Break-even: $1,200k ÷ $99 = <b>12.1k orders a year</b>, against 4k today.</p>"},{"q":"Now account for the 30% of orders that come from depot customers.","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"385.135pt\" height=\"193.048pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 385.135 193.048\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M 0 193.048 L 385.135 193.048 L 385.135 0 L 0 0 L 0 193.048 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"axes_1\"><g id=\"patch_2\"><path d=\"M 31.975 159.456 L 377.935 159.456 L 377.935 9.768 L 31.975 9.768 L 31.975 159.456 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"><g id=\"xtick_1\"><g id=\"line2d_1\"><defs><path id=\"mff7d576334\" d=\"M 0 0 L 0 3.5 \" style=\"stroke: #555555; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></defs><g><use xlink:href=\"#mff7d576334\" x=\"68.211917\" y=\"159.456\" style=\"fill: #555555; stroke: #555555; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_1\"><g style=\"fill: #555555\" transform=\"translate(44.717542 174.184) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-b\" d=\"M 2419 4813 Q 2739 4813 3036 4707 Q 3334 4602 3571 4422 Q 3808 4243 3961 4006 Q 4115 3770 4154 3501 Q 4166 3443 4156 3424 Q 4147 3405 4109 3405 L 3629 3366 Q 3597 3360 3584 3379 Q 3571 3398 3565 3430 Q 3475 3840 3177 4093 Q 2880 4346 2438 4346 Q 1773 4346 1414 3853 Q 1056 3360 1056 2368 Q 1056 1408 1408 915 Q 1760 422 2470 422 Q 2925 422 3229 640 Q 3533 858 3718 1338 Q 3738 1376 3795 1363 L 4173 1274 Q 4192 1267 4205 1248 Q 4218 1229 4205 1184 Q 4154 998 4048 819 Q 3942 640 3788 483 Q 3635 326 3430 201 Q 3226 77 2979 6 Q 2733 -64 2445 -64 Q 1811 -64 1353 230 Q 896 525 656 1075 Q 416 1626 416 2381 Q 416 3136 656 3683 Q 896 4230 1347 4521 Q 1798 4