96 Q 2957 2432 3046 2394 Q 3341 2278 3529 2112 Q 3718 1946 3814 1731 Q 3910 1517 3910 1261 Q 3910 858 3683 557 Q 3456 256 3053 96 Q 2650 -64 2112 -64 Q 1587 -64 1196 83 Q 806 230 598 508 Q 390 787 390 1178 Q 390 1517 560 1789 Q 730 2061 1120 2304 Q 1197 2349 1200 2377 Q 1203 2406 1126 2445 Q 947 2547 809 2688 Q 672 2829 595 3014 Q 518 3200 518 3437 Q 518 3827 720 4137 Q 922 4448 1286 4630 Q 1651 4813 2131 4813 L 2131 4813 z\nM 2138 4365 Q 1850 4365 1613 4249 Q 1376 4134 1238 3939 Q 1101 3744 1101 3488 Q 1101 2906 1760 2758 L 2419 2605 Q 2509 2579 2633 2649 Q 2758 2720 2880 2854 Q 3002 2989 3078 3161 Q 3155 3334 3155 3514 Q 3155 3891 2880 4128 Q 2605 4365 2138 4365 L 2138 4365 z\nM 2144 384 Q 2675 384 2988 614 Q 3302 845 3302 1235 Q 3302 1530 3142 1715 Q 2982 1901 2624 1984 L 1792 2189 Q 1696 2214 1555 2153 Q 1414 2093 1273 1961 Q 1133 1830 1033 1648 Q 934 1466 934 1248 Q 934 838 1244 611 Q 1555 384 2144 384 L 2144 384 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-e3\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-85\" transform=\"translate(55.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-88\" transform=\"translate(121.109375 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_15\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(337.241833 129.521684) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-84\" d=\"M 2470 4678 Q 2502 4717 2534 4733 Q 2566 4749 2630 4749 L 3059 4749 Q 3136 4749 3136 4672 L 3136 1792 Q 3136 1734 3187 1734 L 3789 1734 Q 3878 1734 3878 1670 L 3878 1357 Q 3878 1274 3789 1274 L 3194 1274 Q 3136 1274 3136 1210 L 3136 96 Q 3136 0 3034 0 L 2598 0 Q 2515 0 2515 83 L 2515 1229 Q 2515 1274 2458 1274 L 384 1274 Q 288 1274 288 1357 L 288 1683 Q 288 1728 313 1776 Q 339 1824 390 1894 L 2470 4678 L 2470 4678 z\nM 2445 1734 Q 2502 1734 2502 1779 L 2502 3910 Q 2502 3987 2483 3993 Q 2464 4000 2413 3936 L 851 1818 Q 787 1734 896 1734 L 2445 1734 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-84\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(64.90625 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p4fdd932030\"><rect x=\"31.975\" y=\"9.768\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"149.688\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · What an online order is really worth ($)","note":null},"answer":"<p>A depot customer moving online already earned $209 at the depot. Online, Ironvale now also pays $95 delivery: that order is worth <b>−$95</b> extra.</p> <p>Blended value per online order: 70% × $99 + 30% × (−$95) = <b>$41</b>. Break-even: $1,200k ÷ $41 = <b>29.4k orders</b>.</p> <p>The whole small-builder market is about 54k rentals a year, so break-even needs about <b>54% of every rental</b> in the area. Not realistic.</p> <p>Today, at 4k orders, the platform loses about $1.04M a year.</p>"},{"q":"What if Ironvale charged a $60 delivery fee, as most rivals do?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Each order gains $60: $101 per order, before any benefit from click-and-collect. Break-even falls to <b>11.9k orders</b>, about 22% of the market. Ambitious, but possible over a few years.</p> <p>Some customers will drop off, and depot customers who don't want delivery should be offered free click-and-collect, which removes the cannibalisation cost.</p>"}],"reco":"Don't scale the platform in its current form: free delivery and 30% cannibalisation leave each order worth about $41, so break-even needs about 54% of all small-builder rentals. Keep it, but change the model: charge a $60 delivery fee and offer free click-and-collect, which brings break-even to about 11.9k orders a year (22% of the market). Set a 12-month target and close the platform if order growth stalls below the break-even path. Risk: the fee may slow growth. Next step: test the fee in two postcodes.","great":["Builds profit per order including delivery and marketing","Accounts for cannibalisation of depot orders","Checks break-even against the size of the market","Finds a lever that changes the answer and sets a kill date"],"id":62,"slug":"ironvale-plant-hire"}